WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.270
Star Wars is obsessed with destiny and with
Episode 9 completing the sequel trilogy, Rey

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:11.020
and Kylo Ren's stories come to a dramatic
close with huge reveals about Rey's parents,

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.930
her connection to the Dark Side, and Kylo's
fate.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:18.019
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'll be explaining Rey and Kylo

00:00:18.019 --> 00:00:22.570
Ren's journey in The Rise of Skywalker and
revealing all the hidden clues that foretold

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:23.609
their ultimate destiny.

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:28.119
There will of course be spoilers, so take
care if you haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:33.100
In the very final scene of Episode 9, we see
Rey visit Luke's old home, the Lars homestead

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.690
on Tatooine, where she buries both Luke and
Leia's sabers in honour of their sacrifice

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.570
for the freedom of the galaxy.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.720
She then unveils her own new lightsaber, and
when an old lady asks who she is, Rey replies

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.600
that she's "Rey Skywalker", as the Force Ghosts
of Luke and Leia look upon her.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.010
It's a bold statement that will doubtless
spark debate because Rey isn't a Skywalker

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.010
by blood.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:57.310
What Rey's really doing here though is two-fold.

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:01.740
Firstly, on a personal note, she's showing
her allegiance and adopting the family she

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.350
identifies with over her biological one.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:08.640
Rey is not a Jedi because of her heritage
but because of how she chooses to act and

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.280
who she chooses to be.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:15.090
And secondly, she's taking the legendary family
name and establishing it as an identity or

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.109
title for the future Jedi.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:21.200
And Rey looking out over Tatooine with the
twin suns in the distance is, of course, a

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.979
nostalgic call back to a New Hope when Luke
looked out over the sunset and dreamed of

00:01:25.979 --> 00:01:29.760
adventure, and it signals Rey as the new hope
for future generations.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:35.150
In fact, Rey becoming an honorary or adoptive
Skywalker is something that the new trilogy

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.909
set up early on in The Force Awakens.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:43.370
At Maz Kanata's castle, Rey hears voices from
the basement that lead her to Luke's old lightsaber

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:45.850
that he lost during his duel with Darth Vader.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:48.319
"That lightsaber was Luke's.

00:01:48.319 --> 00:01:49.979
And his father's before him.

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:53.180
And now, it calls to you."

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.369
This is the saber that Rey uses through the
whole of the trilogy and, as Maz mentioned,

00:01:57.369 --> 00:02:00.880
it also originally belonged to Anakin Skywalker.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:05.119
Later in The Force Awakens when Rey and Kylo
Ren battle for control of the lightsaber,

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:11.860
it flies to Rey's hand, not Kylo's even though
he is a Skywalker via his mother Leia's bloodline.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:16.640
And Kylo felt entitled to that Skywalker saber
because of his heritage.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.090
"That lightsaber..
it belongs to me."

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:24.680
He eventually gets to wield it in The Rise
of Skywalker when Rey passes it to him through

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.959
their Force Bond after he arrives on Exogol.

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:31.700
At that point, he's given up the identity
of Kylo Ren, having turned to the light and

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:35.500
become Ben again, making him worthy of wielding
the saber.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:40.840
Rey ultimately defeats the Emperor by combining
that legendary lightsaber with Leia's saber,

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:45.610
which symbolises the passing of the baton
from both the Skywalker siblings as well as

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:50.010
Rey's vital connection with them and their
crucial impact on her character and journey

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.379
in this saga.

00:02:51.379 --> 00:02:55.680
The way Rey crosses the sabers together in
this scene is a moment that visually recalls

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.820
how Luke and Darth Vader crossed lightsabers
as they duelled in front of the Emperor in

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:00.930
Return of the Jedi.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:05.599
And that defensive lightsaber technique which
deflects Palpatine's lightning back to him

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:12.719
reminds me of what Yoda once taught Luke:
"A Jedi uses the Force for knowledge and defense..

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:14.140
never for attack."

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:19.299
Rey embracing the Skywalker legacy as a title
that future Jedi can use and honour also gives

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:22.151
meaning to the title of Episode 9, "The Rise
of Skywalker".

00:03:22.151 --> 00:03:26.239
And is something that Snoke foresaw in The
Force Awakens:

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:31.250
"If Skywalker returns...
the new Jedi will rise."

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:36.370
And by the way, there's also precedence in
the history of our own galaxy of famous family

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:39.450
names becoming titles that future leaders
acquire.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.379
The title of "Caesar" that numerous Roman
Emperors gave themselves was taken from the

00:03:43.379 --> 00:03:47.750
most famous man of that name, "Julius Caesar",
even though they weren't related to him by

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:48.750
blood.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:52.129
The traditional phrase "The king is dead,
long live the king!" is another example of

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:57.140
this idea of continuity with change and the
idea that the "Skywalker" name will now live

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:01.469
on through future generations of Jedi:
"We've passed on all we know.

00:04:01.469 --> 00:04:06.440
A thousand generations live in you now.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.150
We'll always be with you."

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:13.310
And that Jedi legacy is what Rey felt when
the voices of Jedi past called to her, giving

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.480
her the strength to finally defeat Palpatine.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.530
But what about Rey's actual bloodline?

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:23.500
After all, in The Force Awakens, Rey's ancestry
and background was set up as an important

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:26.979
detail to pay attention to:
"Where do you come from?

00:04:26.979 --> 00:04:29.090
Classified, really?

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.090
Me too.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.090
Big secret."

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:35.060
The Last Jedi intriguingly subverted many
fans' expectations when we discovered her

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.060
parents were nobodies.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.800
"So you want to know the truth about your
parents?

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.360
They were filthy junk traders who sold you
off for drinking money."

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:46.220
But similar to Obi-Wan Kenobi's 'certain point
of view' explanation of his original statement

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:50.639
that Darth Vader killed Luke's father, in
Episode 9, Kylo tells Rey that her parents

00:04:50.639 --> 00:04:56.160
chose to be nobodies to protect her as her
father was Palpatine's son, making her a descendant

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.780
of the Emperor, his granddaughter.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:03.150
Rey's link to the Dark Side was strongly hinted
at during her training with Luke in Episode

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:07.260
8, when she discovered she had a powerful
connection with the dark force beneath the

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.260
island.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:09.260
"You went straight to the dark."

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.490
"That place was trying to show me something."

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:12.820
"It offered something you needed."

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.920
"And you didn't even try to stop yourself."

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.970
Luke was terrified of this given his previous
experience with his nephew:

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:24.900
"I've seen this raw strength only once before,
in Ben Solo.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.270
It didn't scare me enough then.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:28.270
It does now."

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:33.360
Episode 9 further develops this theme of Dark
Side Rey when she gives in to anger and accidentally

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.310
lets loose a lightning blast that blows up
a transport ship, thereby revealing her connection

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:39.550
to the Emperor.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:44.550
Lightning blasts are, of course, Palpatine's
signature attack style and Rey even acknowledges

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.669
that the lightning power came from within
her.

00:05:46.669 --> 00:05:51.370
We witness Rey's struggle to contain her anger
and path towards the Dark Side in Episode

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:56.180
9 when she arrives on the wreck of the second
Death Star and enters the old destroyed throne

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.389
room of the Emperor.

00:05:57.389 --> 00:06:02.539
After she picks up the Sith wayfinder, she
has a vision and encounter with a dark version

00:06:02.539 --> 00:06:04.690
of herself who seemingly bests her.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:09.639
The moment has some parallels with Luke's
Dark Side Cave encounter on Dagobah when he

00:06:09.639 --> 00:06:14.700
struck down in anger a vision of Darth Vader
only to reveal his own face underneath the

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:15.700
helmet.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:20.160
And when Kylo confronts her on the Death Star
and destroys the wayfinder, Rey gives in to

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.150
anger again and attacks him.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:27.099
In this duel, Rey's anger fuels her Dark Side
in a similar way to how Luke became enraged

00:06:27.099 --> 00:06:30.220
when he confronted Vader again in Return of
the Jedi.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:31.220
"Good!

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:34.180
Your hate has made you powerful."

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:39.590
And just as Luke chopped off Vader's hand,
Rey attacks Kylo with his own red lightsaber

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:43.169
and stabs him while he's distracted by a Force
call from Leia.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:47.320
It's a crucial moment for Rey who is brought
back from the brink of giving in entirely

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:50.470
to the Dark Side when she senses Leia's passing.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:54.900
And it makes me think of how Luke also pulled
himself back from the Dark Side when the Emperor

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:57.990
tried to goad him into killing his father
Darth Vader.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:02.629
After Rey's failure to control her fear and
anger, she goes to the island to withdraw

00:07:02.629 --> 00:07:04.960
herself from the world as Luke did.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:09.340
Here she's reunited with Luke's Force Ghost
who gives her that crucial third lesson she

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:11.039
seems to have missed in The Last Jedi.

00:07:11.039 --> 00:07:17.500
Luke reminds her that retreating from the
world in fear isn't the answer:

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:22.984
"Confronting fear is the destiny of a Jedi.

00:07:22.984 --> 00:07:24.840
Your destiny"
After all, as Yoda previously told Luke:

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.479
"Anger, fear, aggression.

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:28.990
The dark side of the Force are they."

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:33.770
And Leia told Rey at the beginning of Episode
9 to never be afraid of who she is.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:38.889
Leia already knew Rey was a Palpatine but,
as Luke explains, his sister understood that

00:07:38.889 --> 00:07:43.789
Rey's spirit and heart were more important
and that "some things are stronger than blood."

00:07:43.789 --> 00:07:47.750
And this is perhaps one of the biggest messages
to take away from the these films:

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.330
that no one is or should be completely defined
by their past.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:56.710
After all, Poe is a former spice runner, Finn
and Jannah were both Stormtroopers, and Rey

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:58.039
was a scavenger.

00:07:58.039 --> 00:08:02.300
But more important than their previous lives
or the families they were born into or even

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:07.410
forced into, is the family they later choose
for themselves or adopt as their own.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:13.210
Just as Maz Kanata told Rey in The Force Awakens:
"The belonging you seek is not behind you...

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:14.540
it is ahead."

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:19.509
And Maz followed that up by asking her to
take Luke's lightsaber, a sign that Rey's

00:08:19.509 --> 00:08:23.770
true family and sense of connection would
be with the Skywalkers and the Jedi.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:28.509
By the end of Episode 9, Rey understands this
and rejects Palpatine when he tells her the

00:08:28.509 --> 00:08:33.450
throne is her birthright and she instead allies
herself with Ben to stand against the Emperor

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.800
and the Sith.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.750
To understand Kylo Ren's redemptive arc, we
need to go back to the beginning of The Force

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:42.970
Awakens where we find him already conflicted
in his feelings of allegiance to the Dark

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:43.970
Side.

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:44.970
"Forgive me.

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:46.670
I feel it again.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.650
The call to the light.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:49.970
Supreme Leader senses it.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:50.970
Show me again.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:52.590
The power of the darkness."

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:57.890
In fact, there's an intriguing message underlying
what Rey says to Kylo after he captures her

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:59.980
in The Force Awakens:
"You're afraid.

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:03.870
That you will never be as strong as Darth
Vader."

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:08.000
The hidden meaning in this line is that although
Vader was a villain, he eventually found the

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.970
strength to turn back to the Light Side and
stand against the Emperor.

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:17.000
Kylo, however, believes he needs to be strong
to embrace the Dark Side, which we see in

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.190
what he says to his father Han Solo just before
killing him:

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:24.100
"I know what I have to do but I don't know
if I have the strength to do it."

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:30.310
But in Episode 9, Kylo eventually finds true
strength when he talks to his father again

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.620
after his battle with Rey on the Death Star.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:38.640
Han, who appears as one of his memories, reminds
him that Ben isn't dead, but Kylo Ren is.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.110
And using the same words that he said to his
father on Starkiller Base, Ben now throws

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:48.680
his lightsaber into the water, finally rejecting
his Dark Side identity of Kylo Ren.

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:53.130
That eventual redemption for him began in
The Last Jedi, where Rey felt that the connection

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.790
she was beginning to establish through their
Force Bond meant he could still be turned

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:58.060
back to the Light Side.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:01.589
"You failed him by thinking his choice was
already made.

00:10:01.589 --> 00:10:02.589
It wasn't.

00:10:02.589 --> 00:10:03.880
There's still conflict in him.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:11.200
Just now when we touched hands,
I saw his future.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:13.390
Then he's our last hope."

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:17.900
And Ben does become Rey's last hope when he
stands with her against the Emperor and then

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:22.290
brings her back by Force healing her after
she collapses from the exertion of killing

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:23.399
Palpatine.

00:10:23.399 --> 00:10:27.840
It was also Kylo's connection with his mother
Leia that kept him from fully turning to the

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:28.840
Dark Side.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:32.720
In The Last Jedi, he stopped himself from
firing upon Leia's ship when he sensed her

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:33.720
presence.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:38.070
And that moment is revisited in The Rise of
Skywalker when Leia calls to him and stops

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:42.589
him from delivering a fatal blow to Rey during
their duel on the Death Star.

00:10:42.589 --> 00:10:46.750
Together both Leia and Han bring their son
back, something that Leia told Han they would

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:50.830
do in The Force Awakens:
"We can still save him.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:51.830
Me.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:52.830
You."

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:57.930
So basically, what Lor San Tekka told Kylo
at the very beginning of the sequel trilogy

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:59.500
turned out to be right.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:02.790
"You cannot deny the truth that is your family.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:05.420
I know where you come from.

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:07.370
Before you called yourself Kylo Ren."

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:12.890
Ultimately, his Kylo Ren alter ego has been
a performance, a big act by a person trying

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:16.480
to take on the enormous mantle of the infamous
Darth Vader.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:19.730
Unlike Vader though, Kylo didn't require his
helmet to survive.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:27.490
"Take off that mask, you don't need it"
It was just another way to conceal who he

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:32.130
really was, while he tried every way he could
to be something he ultimately wasn't:

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:40.010
"You're no Vader, you're just a child in a
mask."

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:44.269
So although Kylo Ren had worshipped the legend
of the Sith Lord Darth Vader.

00:11:44.269 --> 00:11:47.670
"Show me grandfather, and I will finish what
you started."

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:52.800
By the end, like Anakin, Ben rejects the Emperor
and the way of the Sith and redeems himself.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:57.889
Now, how do you feel about Rey and Kylo's
endings in The Rise of Skywalker and their

00:11:57.889 --> 00:11:59.990
arcs through the sequel trilogy?

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:04.670
Comment with your thoughts below and if you
enjoyed this video a thumbs-up is hugely appreciated

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:07.889
and don't forget to subscribe to get all my
new videos.

00:12:07.889 --> 00:12:12.450
Tap left for my next Star Wars video or tap
right for another video you're sure to like.

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:14.850
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:16.259
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

